WEBVTT

00:06.541 --> 00:10.750
Kyohachi-ryu School,
the origin of swordsmanship.

00:10.833 --> 00:17.833
Its legend was believed
to have ended long ago.

00:17.916 --> 00:24.916
Yet eight successors lived on,
silently immersing themselves in training.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.208
Don't screw with me!

00:55.291 --> 00:57.833
What's wrong, Iroha?
Is that all you've got?

00:58.416 --> 01:00.000
Shut up, Sansuke!

01:27.833 --> 01:29.500
You win, Shikura.

01:29.583 --> 01:32.416
If you were playing seriously,
it'd be a different story.

01:41.541 --> 01:42.708
Another one for me.

01:42.791 --> 01:45.416
Huh? You're going
for another round, Jinroku?

01:45.500 --> 01:48.166
You've had, what, ten bowls?

01:48.250 --> 01:49.291
Amazing.

01:49.375 --> 01:52.291
By the way, I heard Satsuma
and Choshu have joined forces.

01:52.375 --> 01:55.291
I wonder if the Edo shogunate
or the anti-shogunate will win.

01:55.375 --> 01:58.125
Obviously whichever side
knows how to use us effectively.

01:58.208 --> 02:00.083
-Right, Shu-nii?
-Yeah, that's right.

02:00.583 --> 02:02.000
Can we join the war too?

02:02.083 --> 02:04.083
That's for Master to decide.

02:04.166 --> 02:07.916
I can't wait to fight.
We've trained so hard all these years.

02:08.000 --> 02:10.750
Oh, please.
Any side Sansuke joins is gonna lose.

02:10.833 --> 02:14.291
Come on, Iroha. You're the one who cries
when I beat you in training.

02:14.375 --> 02:15.208
What?

02:15.708 --> 02:17.583
Look who's talking.

02:17.666 --> 02:20.875
-You tripped earlier too, remember?
-Huh? I didn't trip.

02:30.250 --> 02:31.416
I know.

02:32.541 --> 02:34.333
I don't have much time left.

02:37.541 --> 02:38.541
It's tomorrow.

03:11.000 --> 03:14.166
There is something I must tell you all.

03:15.666 --> 03:21.083
You have endured harsh training together
for nearly ten years.

03:23.500 --> 03:24.416
But…

03:26.333 --> 03:28.416
that ends today.

03:32.875 --> 03:37.583
The Kyohachi-ryu School shall be
passed down to a single successor.

03:40.458 --> 03:44.208
Only one person can inherit it.

03:47.666 --> 03:48.916
You must kill each other.

03:52.291 --> 03:56.125
You will begin tomorrow
when the sun reaches due south.

03:56.958 --> 04:00.166
You must forget that you are siblings.

04:01.250 --> 04:03.583
No one is allowed to flee.

04:19.708 --> 04:21.041
This is our fate.

04:23.250 --> 04:24.875
We all knew it would come to this.

04:25.875 --> 04:26.708
Listen,

04:27.791 --> 04:29.458
why don't we leave the mountain?

04:30.000 --> 04:33.208
We could live somewhere secluded,
where Master won't find us.

04:33.291 --> 04:35.000
-As long as we're together--
-No.

04:35.083 --> 04:36.416
Gentosai will come after us.

04:36.500 --> 04:38.583
Master was just trying to scare us.

04:38.666 --> 04:40.625
No, he's out there.

04:40.708 --> 04:44.833
I once saw him talking with Master.

04:46.541 --> 04:49.958
That man… is a monster.

04:51.833 --> 04:54.375
Ever since we mastered
the art of the Kyohachi-ryu School,

04:54.458 --> 04:56.791
we have known this day would come.

04:57.708 --> 04:58.708
This…

04:59.916 --> 05:02.083
is our fate.

05:02.666 --> 05:03.583
Yes.

05:08.208 --> 05:09.083
We have no choice.

05:30.333 --> 05:31.375
Shu-nii…

05:36.125 --> 05:37.666
What should we do?

06:56.208 --> 06:58.083
Well, well…

07:15.833 --> 07:18.125
So, how many casualties on our side?

07:18.208 --> 07:19.541
We lost 15.

07:20.833 --> 07:23.750
Kokushu the Manslayer
is absolutely insane.

07:24.708 --> 07:26.125
What did the organizer say?

07:26.208 --> 07:31.500
The rules do not explicitly forbid
killing our troops, so the game continues.

07:31.583 --> 07:33.916
How unexpected.

07:34.416 --> 07:37.250
Shujiro Saga has already been informed.

07:40.708 --> 07:43.708
A total of 192 participants
have been eliminated.

07:43.791 --> 07:47.041
Also, number 19, Ukyo Kikuomi,
the first to leave Tenryuji Temple,

07:47.125 --> 07:49.041
has been eliminated.

07:49.125 --> 07:50.416
What a shame.

07:50.500 --> 07:54.208
Reportedly, he lost in a duel
against Bukotsu Kanjiya.

07:54.291 --> 07:59.416
Bukotsu the Savage Slasher.
He looks like another promising player.

08:02.250 --> 08:05.875
Gentlemen, if you're ready,
shall we begin?

08:07.500 --> 08:11.625
Of course. That's what
we're all here to enjoy, isn't it?

08:13.208 --> 08:17.375
Now then, allow me to explain
the betting process once more.

08:17.458 --> 08:19.625
What you'll be predicting is

08:19.708 --> 08:23.250
which participant will be the first
to pass through the next post station.

08:23.750 --> 08:26.791
Our opening bet is on
the first participant to pass Seki-juku,

08:26.875 --> 08:29.208
after crossing the Suzuka Pass.

08:29.291 --> 08:31.541
Place your bets, everyone.

08:34.041 --> 08:36.541
My bet's on number 66, Bukotsu Kanjiya.

08:36.625 --> 08:38.500
The Suzuka Pass is no easy path.

08:38.583 --> 08:41.833
You won't get through a fight this fierce
without his level of skill.

08:41.916 --> 08:44.916
Number 200, Naoto Yoshida.
Number 201, Shoji Yoshida.

08:45.000 --> 08:46.750
Oh, yes…

08:46.833 --> 08:49.083
The spear twins.

08:49.166 --> 08:51.041
Mr. Sakakibara likes to be unconventional.

08:51.125 --> 08:53.583
Their spear work
at Tenryuji Temple was exceptional.

08:53.666 --> 08:56.041
A solid bet, I'd say.

08:56.708 --> 08:58.458
Number 33, Kyojin Tsuge.

08:58.541 --> 09:00.875
Oh? As for me,

09:00.958 --> 09:03.333
I'll go with number 108, Shujiro Saga.

09:05.333 --> 09:07.083
All bets are now on the table.

09:07.166 --> 09:10.708
Let us proceed with the first round.

09:10.791 --> 09:12.708
Please enjoy to your heart's content.

09:21.458 --> 09:25.541
SUZUKA PASS, MIE

09:43.083 --> 09:44.500
The mountain pass begins here.

09:45.458 --> 09:47.958
You won't get to Seki-juku
without crossing it.

09:48.458 --> 09:51.500
There will be a lot of participants here.
Stay close.

09:53.541 --> 09:54.375
Yes, sir.

09:59.875 --> 10:00.875
What's the matter?

10:07.041 --> 10:10.791
"Kokushu the Manslayer,"
a man who knew only how to kill.

10:13.916 --> 10:17.625
What has your life been like, Shujiro?

10:20.750 --> 10:21.875
I…

10:23.666 --> 10:26.291
I grew up in the mountains
with my siblings.

10:27.291 --> 10:28.208
Siblings?

10:28.875 --> 10:33.125
We were all orphans taken in by Master.
We shared no blood ties.

10:34.500 --> 10:35.666
And there,

10:37.458 --> 10:40.666
we learned nothing but how to kill.

10:45.333 --> 10:47.666
Did you live there all your life?

10:47.750 --> 10:52.416
No. After that, I cut down men in Kyoto
as a bodyguard for the Satsuma domain.

10:54.125 --> 10:58.375
I kept killing through the war,
and before I knew it…

11:00.583 --> 11:03.166
they were calling me
Kokushu the Manslayer.

11:41.708 --> 11:42.916
Stay alert.

11:57.083 --> 11:58.583
You survived Tenryuji Temple?

12:00.208 --> 12:03.250
You? You're with a child
and can't even draw your sword.

12:32.625 --> 12:33.875
Naoto!

12:35.166 --> 12:36.833
Futaba, run!

12:54.208 --> 12:55.583
Futaba!

13:02.166 --> 13:03.750
-Are you all right?
-Yes.

13:17.416 --> 13:18.625
Is this…

13:26.666 --> 13:27.833
Someone's nearby.

13:40.166 --> 13:43.000
I've been waiting
a long time for you, Shujiro Saga.

13:43.083 --> 13:44.458
Iroha!

13:44.541 --> 13:46.750
Stop! I won't fight my little sister!

13:46.833 --> 13:48.375
Save your words!

13:48.916 --> 13:52.541
Do you have any idea
what happened to us because of you?

13:55.166 --> 13:58.166
Can you imagine what your own
brothers felt when you left them behind?!

13:59.208 --> 14:00.250
Since I left the mountain,

14:00.333 --> 14:03.666
I've lived every day as if I were dead.

14:06.791 --> 14:08.166
I'm sorry.

14:49.333 --> 14:50.333
Move back!

14:50.416 --> 14:51.708
Iroha!

14:52.208 --> 14:53.375
Come.

14:59.833 --> 15:01.416
Iroha, go in front!

15:45.625 --> 15:48.375
Defend yourself. Unless you want to die.

16:12.041 --> 16:13.208
Get closer!

16:17.375 --> 16:18.958
Surround them! Closer!

16:19.750 --> 16:21.250
-Move up!
-Closer!

16:22.875 --> 16:24.333
No! Get back here!

16:27.333 --> 16:28.458
Gojiro!

16:28.541 --> 16:29.916
Stay back! Keep your distance!

16:32.125 --> 16:33.416
Aim for the brat!

16:33.500 --> 16:35.333
That brat! Go after her!

16:52.208 --> 16:54.416
Take down the brat and the woman!

17:22.375 --> 17:23.291
Who is he?

17:27.416 --> 17:28.708
He's gonna kill me!

17:44.958 --> 17:46.250
Sheathe your sword.

17:48.583 --> 17:50.166
Why did you help us?

17:52.500 --> 17:54.041
Among our people,

17:56.333 --> 18:00.000
taking the life of a child
is believed to be the greatest evil.

18:00.708 --> 18:05.166
We honor those who shield children
and do not wish to fight them.

18:05.250 --> 18:07.583
Why would we believe you so easily?

18:19.125 --> 18:20.208
Wait…

18:24.250 --> 18:25.833
Thank you.

18:28.000 --> 18:29.458
May I ask your name?

18:31.416 --> 18:32.666
Kamuykocha.

18:36.958 --> 18:39.583
As long as that child is with you,
I will not strike.

18:43.750 --> 18:45.625
Kamuykocha…

18:46.375 --> 18:48.250
-He's Ainu.
-Ainu?

18:48.333 --> 18:50.125
The indigenous people of Hokkaido.

18:50.208 --> 18:52.208
I saw them at the Battle of Hakodate.

18:52.875 --> 18:56.541
So it's true that the newspapers
made it all the way to Hokkaido.

19:00.750 --> 19:02.833
We can pass through Seki-juku with these.

19:03.833 --> 19:05.916
More participants
will be coming from behind.

19:06.000 --> 19:07.125
We need to hurry.

19:10.375 --> 19:11.666
Iroha,

19:12.250 --> 19:13.291
take this one.

19:20.208 --> 19:22.166
If you really want to kill me,

19:23.333 --> 19:24.958
then do it in Tokyo.

19:37.000 --> 19:38.000
Wait.

19:42.375 --> 19:43.875
I'll go with you.

19:50.666 --> 19:52.916
There's still something you need to do.

19:55.791 --> 19:57.666
You can't just walk away from it.

20:04.875 --> 20:05.958
All right.

20:21.125 --> 20:22.541
Is one enough?

20:22.625 --> 20:24.541
Carrying too many is risky. Let's move.

20:24.625 --> 20:25.500
Yes.

20:45.958 --> 20:46.875
Come in.

20:50.375 --> 20:51.750
Pardon the intrusion.

20:52.291 --> 20:54.708
I'm here to report
on the investigation progress.

20:55.291 --> 20:56.916
The Kyoto Prefectural Office

20:57.000 --> 20:59.708
has discovered bloodstains
and dismembered human remains.

20:59.791 --> 21:02.166
They reported numerous eyewitness accounts

21:02.250 --> 21:05.458
of sword duels involving individuals
believed to be shizoku.

21:06.833 --> 21:09.333
Furthermore, the location
of the eyewitness accounts

21:09.416 --> 21:14.458
has been gradually shifting over time,
from Shiga to Mie.

21:14.541 --> 21:17.458
You're saying the shizoku
are fighting with each other as they move?

21:17.541 --> 21:18.666
Indeed.

21:19.250 --> 21:20.291
And…

21:21.416 --> 21:24.250
they appear to be
heading toward Tokyo from Kyoto.

21:25.166 --> 21:27.000
At least that's how it looks.

21:27.083 --> 21:29.041
So they're moving toward us?

21:29.125 --> 21:30.791
There's more.

21:30.875 --> 21:34.458
The reports say numerous gunshots
were heard at Tenryuji Temple.

21:36.500 --> 21:37.666
Lord Okubo.

21:37.750 --> 21:42.291
A large number of shizoku armed with guns
and swords are approaching Tokyo.

21:42.375 --> 21:46.958
Which implies that discontented shizoku
are plotting a civil uprising--

21:47.041 --> 21:51.166
If they were plotting a civil uprising,
they wouldn't need to cut each other down.

21:51.250 --> 21:52.125
But sir…

21:57.041 --> 21:58.083
I understand.

21:59.375 --> 22:01.958
If ignored, it may escalate
into a national crisis.

22:02.458 --> 22:06.083
Kawaji, track down the source
of the guns immediately.

22:06.166 --> 22:09.708
Maejima, analyze all telegram
communications from the past month.

22:09.791 --> 22:12.333
-There might be traces left behind.
-Yes, sir.

22:26.250 --> 22:28.041
TENRYUJI TEMPLE

22:34.125 --> 22:37.166
SEKI

22:46.666 --> 22:49.083
SEKI-JUKU

22:49.166 --> 22:51.958
REQUIRED POINTS: THREE

23:03.875 --> 23:05.958
We're almost at the exit.

23:06.041 --> 23:08.375
There should be someone here
to check our tags.

23:36.250 --> 23:38.166
No need to be so wary.

23:39.500 --> 23:42.458
I am Tsurubami,
in charge of overseeing your passage.

23:43.208 --> 23:44.833
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

23:48.416 --> 23:49.875
Now, your wooden tags, please.

23:59.708 --> 24:02.000
Shujiro Saga, three points.

24:02.958 --> 24:04.458
Futaba Katsuki, three points.

24:05.083 --> 24:07.041
Iroha Kinugasa, five points.

24:08.875 --> 24:10.916
You are all cleared to pass.

24:13.083 --> 24:14.958
This is for you, Miss Kinugasa.

24:18.333 --> 24:20.416
This red tag counts for three points.

24:21.000 --> 24:24.250
In exchange, hand over three tags
other than the one around your neck.

24:26.083 --> 24:27.083
Tsurubami, was it?

24:28.958 --> 24:29.791
Yes.

24:29.875 --> 24:31.750
What is the purpose of this game?

24:31.833 --> 24:32.875
I cannot answer that.

24:32.958 --> 24:34.333
Let me put it another way.

24:36.291 --> 24:37.791
Who are you people?

24:37.875 --> 24:39.583
I cannot answer that either.

24:40.083 --> 24:41.125
That said…

24:43.625 --> 24:49.250
I believe you and Kinugasa
are well acquainted with "Kodoku."

24:51.458 --> 24:52.833
What are you implying?

24:55.291 --> 24:56.583
Three bugs.

25:05.041 --> 25:08.125
Well then, may your journey go well.

25:32.208 --> 25:33.208
Gentlemen,

25:34.916 --> 25:38.166
we've confirmed all participants
have passed through Seki-juku.

25:38.250 --> 25:40.250
And the result?

25:40.333 --> 25:42.750
The first participant to reach Seki-juku…

25:44.708 --> 25:46.166
was number 33, Kyojin Tsuge.

25:46.250 --> 25:47.250
Yes!

25:49.833 --> 25:52.958
Looks like I've won this round.

25:54.000 --> 25:55.000
Darn it!

25:56.458 --> 25:57.958
Well, I'll be damned.

25:58.458 --> 26:00.333
No surprise for a former ninja from Iga.

26:01.333 --> 26:04.833
Morosawa, maybe we went a little too far
taking a long shot, huh?

26:05.416 --> 26:06.750
It's only the first round.

26:06.833 --> 26:08.833
We've got plenty
of chances left to recover.

26:08.916 --> 26:10.083
I see.

26:10.166 --> 26:12.916
And then there's number 277, Kamuykocha.

26:13.000 --> 26:14.958
I never expected
the Ainu to join this game.

26:15.041 --> 26:19.083
Well now, this is getting unpredictable.

26:19.166 --> 26:22.625
Honestly, I can't be
thankful enough to the organizer

26:23.375 --> 26:25.500
for providing us with so much fun.

26:25.583 --> 26:27.166
Much obliged.

26:27.250 --> 26:31.083
Now then, let us proceed
with the second bet.

26:31.750 --> 26:33.583
Our second bet is on the first participant

26:33.666 --> 26:36.500
to pass through
the next checkpoint, Chiryu-juku.

26:43.250 --> 26:47.958
YOKKAICHI-JUKU

26:59.000 --> 27:00.458
You must be Mr. Saga.

27:01.458 --> 27:05.083
We've been expecting you. Please, come in.

27:20.958 --> 27:22.458
I knew you'd show up.

27:23.083 --> 27:26.833
No surprise. A seasoned warrior
like you has a sharp sense of survival.

27:27.583 --> 27:29.250
Why did you choose Yokkaichi?

27:29.333 --> 27:31.416
I told you I'm a strategist, remember?

27:31.500 --> 27:33.458
The Suzuka Pass is no easy path.

27:33.958 --> 27:37.541
Bringing along a girl who can't even
fight must've been a pain, huh?

27:38.291 --> 27:42.041
I figured it must be about time
you're hoping to form an alliance.

27:45.166 --> 27:46.000
What's this?

27:46.541 --> 27:50.333
Not just the little miss, huh?
You've got quite the beauty tagging along.

27:50.416 --> 27:53.666
-Quiet.
-Don't count on it. Kyojin here.

27:54.416 --> 27:57.416
Pleased to meet you, Iroha Kinugasa.

27:58.083 --> 27:59.541
How do you know my name?

28:00.500 --> 28:02.791
Like I said, I'm a strategist.

28:06.250 --> 28:07.291
Kyojin.

28:10.583 --> 28:12.875
I do not trust you.

28:13.875 --> 28:14.833
However…

28:16.416 --> 28:19.083
I came here to improve
my chances of survival.

28:22.291 --> 28:24.125
Do you know what Kodoku really means?

28:27.000 --> 28:28.625
Three bugs, right?

28:29.333 --> 28:30.166
Yeah.

28:34.083 --> 28:37.916
This is how you write Kodoku.

28:41.875 --> 28:45.333
A hundred insects are sealed in a jar
and made to fight to the death.

28:46.250 --> 28:49.041
Only the last one left alive
becomes a god

28:49.583 --> 28:52.083
and gains the power to slaughter all.

28:53.333 --> 28:55.250
You know your stuff.

28:57.708 --> 28:59.625
Once, Iroha and I…

29:01.041 --> 29:03.041
were bugs inside that jar.

29:16.083 --> 29:19.750
So this is your second time?
You two lead quite the life.

29:23.458 --> 29:28.166
Well, anyway, if this really
is that type of Kodoku,

29:28.750 --> 29:32.375
it means only one person
will survive to the end.

29:34.333 --> 29:37.958
Are you prepared to kill

29:39.708 --> 29:41.791
those you once fought alongside?

29:46.250 --> 29:48.833
I've got someone I need to save.

29:50.750 --> 29:51.916
But…

29:53.416 --> 29:56.166
It doesn't mean I'm going to play
this game on their terms.

30:03.458 --> 30:06.791
Looks like I was right
to reach out to you.

30:09.333 --> 30:13.375
We're allies now, Kokushu Saga.

30:18.125 --> 30:19.500
What's that?

30:19.583 --> 30:23.125
It's called a handshake.
You just grab each other's hands.

30:23.208 --> 30:24.458
It's a foreign greeting.

30:24.541 --> 30:28.041
It means, "I'm not holding anything
in my hands and I trust you."

30:40.833 --> 30:41.833
You too, little miss.

30:45.916 --> 30:46.916
I'm Futaba Katsuki.

30:47.000 --> 30:48.250
A pleasure.

30:50.333 --> 30:51.333
What is it?

30:52.000 --> 30:55.833
Making us kill each other like this…

30:56.958 --> 30:58.958
What does the organizer really want?

31:00.083 --> 31:02.208
Even offering such a huge sum of money.

31:03.875 --> 31:06.708
Exactly. That's the real problem.

31:06.791 --> 31:09.125
If we don't learn
what they're really after,

31:09.208 --> 31:12.500
we'll end up dancing
in the palm of their hand.

31:13.208 --> 31:15.291
So you've got a plan?

31:16.041 --> 31:19.541
That's why I brought up
the idea of an alliance.

31:19.625 --> 31:21.541
What exactly are you planning?

31:24.583 --> 31:27.458
We're going to find out
what this Kodoku really is.

31:28.500 --> 31:31.208
And to do that,
I want to run an experiment.

31:31.291 --> 31:32.791
An experiment?

31:37.000 --> 31:38.708
Well, I'll explain the details tomorrow.

31:38.791 --> 31:41.041
Something to look forward to.

31:41.916 --> 31:44.041
Make sure you get a good rest today, okay?

31:51.791 --> 31:55.833
KODOKU

31:55.916 --> 31:57.250
You must kill each other.

32:44.666 --> 32:45.791
Shu-nii.

32:48.625 --> 32:49.625
Where are you going?

32:51.916 --> 32:53.166
The bathroom.

33:34.500 --> 33:35.583
No…

33:38.250 --> 33:39.416
Gentosai?

34:44.916 --> 34:46.791
Why are you traveling with that child?

34:50.583 --> 34:54.208
We met at Tenryuji Temple
and have been traveling together since.

34:54.291 --> 34:55.458
That's all.

34:56.750 --> 34:59.041
You really think she can survive this?

35:06.833 --> 35:08.750
After leaving us behind,

35:10.875 --> 35:12.708
is this some kind of atonement?

35:33.291 --> 35:34.458
Iroha,

35:36.416 --> 35:38.458
what happened after I left?

35:39.458 --> 35:40.833
Please tell me.

35:48.583 --> 35:49.833
Master…

35:51.583 --> 35:54.583
He feared the techniques
of Kyohachi-ryu School might be leaked.

35:55.583 --> 35:57.541
So he tried to kill us all.

36:01.541 --> 36:03.166
Ikkan-nii…

36:04.750 --> 36:08.500
He stood up to Master so we could escape.

36:11.833 --> 36:14.958
Thanks to him, we were able
to get off the mountain.

36:17.041 --> 36:18.416
We were scattered.

36:22.666 --> 36:25.875
Just because I am a woman,
I wasn't allowed to hold a sword.

36:31.750 --> 36:33.250
I've spent my life

36:35.333 --> 36:37.250
running from Gentosai.

36:42.208 --> 36:43.791
Everything that happened

36:45.250 --> 36:47.750
is all because you ran away back then.

36:59.166 --> 37:00.375
Please forgive me.

37:16.500 --> 37:18.291
Why did you join Kodoku?

37:21.250 --> 37:23.500
My wife is suffering from cholera.

37:25.666 --> 37:27.166
My daughter is dead.

37:28.791 --> 37:31.583
It's only a matter of time
before my son becomes sick too.

37:32.333 --> 37:34.250
But I don't have the money for medicine.

37:34.333 --> 37:35.333
I see.

37:38.000 --> 37:40.125
So you're a father now.

37:43.583 --> 37:44.458
And you, Iroha?

37:46.291 --> 37:48.125
Why did you join Kodoku?

37:50.791 --> 37:53.166
You told me I still
have something I need to do.

37:58.916 --> 38:01.000
I'm not sure if I want to involve you.

38:03.833 --> 38:05.500
I need to think more.

38:19.208 --> 38:20.375
Iroha.

38:26.208 --> 38:28.125
I ran away back then.

38:32.000 --> 38:38.000
But I have no intention of running

38:39.541 --> 38:41.375
from the suffering I caused you all.

38:43.125 --> 38:44.041
And yet,

38:45.791 --> 38:48.250
getting to see you again, alive…

38:52.875 --> 38:54.625
is something I'm truly grateful for.

39:19.000 --> 39:21.083
We need two more to pass through Chiryu.

39:21.916 --> 39:24.791
I guess we should win them now,
while there are plenty around.

39:24.875 --> 39:26.666
There's a ferry at Miya-juku.

39:27.500 --> 39:29.083
The participants are bound to--

39:43.416 --> 39:44.708
Your face.

39:45.333 --> 39:46.208
What?

39:50.833 --> 39:53.166
Maybe I was wrong.

39:54.041 --> 39:56.125
What's this guy mumbling about?

40:46.041 --> 40:49.583
Not here either…

41:20.541 --> 41:22.166
Gentosai.

41:27.416 --> 41:28.666
Any leads?

41:29.166 --> 41:30.000
Yes.

41:37.708 --> 41:38.708
Enter.

41:41.166 --> 41:44.333
-We've identified where the guns are from.
-Where?

41:44.416 --> 41:47.833
When we looked into the records
from the smuggler we arrested recently,

41:48.416 --> 41:52.208
we confirmed that a large shipment
was brought in from Britain to Yokohama.

41:57.166 --> 42:01.166
The shipment contained
over a hundred Snider rifles.

42:01.958 --> 42:07.041
Impossible. A lone smuggler couldn't
possibly afford that many rifles.

42:07.916 --> 42:10.750
Right. It seems he had clients.

42:11.833 --> 42:12.708
Who?

42:18.500 --> 42:19.416
Mitsui.

42:21.666 --> 42:22.625
Sumitomo.

42:25.083 --> 42:26.208
Yasuda.

42:28.125 --> 42:29.291
Mitsubishi.

42:30.625 --> 42:32.833
Behind this incident…

42:35.416 --> 42:41.083
are the four powerful zaibatsu
supporting the Meiji government.

43:05.750 --> 43:08.958
95 REMAINING

46:48.250 --> 46:51.750
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
